{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1504524-im-gonna-stupid-rewriting-the-dang-thang-journal","id":1504524,"title":"Im gonna Stupid/Rewriting the dang thang Journal","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-05T19:03:44-08:00","id":1504524,"title":"Im gonna Stupid/Rewriting the dang thang Journal","content":"So this my personal journal to hell, after attempting to read and convince someone to play, Ive decided to just suck it up and accept the fact that no rational person will want to even touch Exalted 3rd edition. My personal copy it self refused to play and lept from off its own spine, but I assume that's more of an issue the book became a uncontrolled mess during development and suffered Kickstarter bloat.<br /> So its time to go back and figure out what I liked and what bothered me. First and foremost, The book is too big and too complicated. I didn't like the charm set, too much redundancy and way too hard to navigate. The Lore, some of it I felt moved in an interesting direction and others it kind of suffered that old White Wolf Cringe.<br /> First and foremost Im going back to the old metaphysics of Creation, that motonic physics, that kind that lead to Magitech. The wishy washy miracle style nonsense gives me gas, and comes across as sophomoric and very much in the anti-science vein that a lot of old World of Darkness games had, and that always gave me indigestion. So thaumaturgy goes back to being a thing any one can learn or do but requires education and training. To me Thaumaturgy was that special thing that mortals had, that was taught to them by the Dragon Kings, not Exalted Light special power you have to be born with.<br /> <br /> The big fix from the previous version of Occult (the big it can do anything skill along with Lore) is to apply the old, it was sitting infront of our face solution. Im using Craft. Like Craft, Occult and Lore are going to have lots of subskills under its umbrella that you have to learn, but Charms are generally unlocked by the highest rated subskill.<br /> <br /> The First branch of powers I'm going to be working on getting working will be Mortal Heroes, then Dragon Blooded. For Rules system I'm going to be looking at both Story Path, and Story Telling. And maybe I'll figure out how to make a economic model that makes sense. <br /> But my point is, Exalted was once my favorite fantasy setting for RPG, but I figured we lost what it was. The first was when the guys who took over clearly did not care for Anime and dropped mention of them as inspiration for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T07:14:04-08:00","id":1504753,"title":"","content":"The first thing that I missed from previous edition of Exalted was the loss of Virtues. Compassion, Conviction, Temperance, and Valor. There is a prevailing theory in modern Roleplay nothing should interfere with your sense of freewill. The problem is that this often leads to murder hoboism and modern sensibilities when exploring &quot;foreign&quot; cultures and a degree of ethnocentrism. Applying these internal gauges can really direct players to engage in different ways of thinking.<br /> it's why I am going to borrow/steal a mechanic from one of the greatest RPGs King Arthur Pendragon, the Traits and Passions mechanic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Essentially intimacies and virtues are going to be rated on 5 point scale. During each session you can channel each one once to generate extra successes for a point of willpower to assist in any action. These can also act as defense against mental/social manipulations. The problem lies when you fail these checks you are channeling or have to act against them. In those situations you looking at either gaining a point of limit or degrading a intimacy. So for example let's say I have a high Valor and some one is challenging me to a fight or calling me a coward. I roll to see if my Valor gets me to accept the fight, now I'm not required to accept and take no penalty if I fail the Valor check, but if I get any successes with the Valor check, I am considering the following house rules: have to take a point of Limit and every success does a point of Willpower damage, temporarily depleting my will, if I have no will each extra point of unabsorbed will damage (will damage in excess of total will power) causes an additional point of Limit. Taking will damage does limit the max amount of will power you can have. <br /> will post more today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T07:57:43-08:00","id":1504937,"title":"","content":"&quot;...No rational person would want to even touch 3rd edition...<br /> *laughs bitterly in forever ST while running multiple multi-year chronicles *<br /> <br /> That aside, you'd probably actually like the virtue/Intimacy system in Exalted Essence. It provides a lot of the more rigid characterization you're missing without falling into 1E/2E's trap of &quot;having lower Virtues is objectively less powerful.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T09:44:50-08:00","id":1504948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1504524-im-gonna-stupid-rewriting-the-dang-thang-journal?p=1504937#post1504937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;...No rational person would want to even touch 3rd edition...<br /> *laughs bitterly in forever ST while running multiple multi-year chronicles *<br /> <br /> That aside, you'd probably actually like the virtue/Intimacy system in Exalted Essence. It provides a lot of the more rigid characterization you're missing without falling into 1E/2E's trap of &quot;having lower Virtues is objectively less powerful.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well they are less powerful, but there is a price for power the pull of the Virtues on your behavior, which is why I'm tying passions/intimacies and virtues together more tightly. The issue is that we want more power but with out the baggage. If we accept the baggage, that the power comes with a price, and that it will cause tragedy then great stories are to be had. Many of the great epics had misfortune and tragedy, and having that be more tied to the game is something to milk, and Limit has it somewhat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}